From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:52:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 69/73] fix(gastown): make the default-branch fetch safe under
 set -e (gcp-5ddt)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review touch-up on the resolution block added in the previous commit.
The refresh was written as `[ -n "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" ] && git fetch ...`,
which evaluates to non-zero whenever the variable is empty — the exact
case the next line is there to handle. Under `set -e` that aborts the
step before the fail-closed branch can run, turning a graceful skip into
an abandoned patrol leg. The `git fetch` itself is likewise best-effort:
the ref is verified with `git rev-parse` immediately afterwards, so a
transient fetch failure should fall into that check rather than kill the
step.

Rewritten as a plain `if` with `|| true` on the fetch. Behaviour is
otherwise unchanged; the guard still fails closed when the branch cannot
be resolved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
index 53a0cbc..46066ff 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
@@ -351,7 +351,9 @@ if [ -z "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" ]; then
   DEFAULT_BRANCH=$(git ls-remote --symref origin HEAD 2>/dev/null |
     awk '$1 == "ref:" { sub("refs/heads/", "", $2); print $2; exit }')
 fi
-[ -n "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" ] && git fetch origin "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" >/dev/null 2>&1
+if [ -n "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" ]; then
+  git fetch origin "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+fi
 if [ -z "$DEFAULT_BRANCH" ] ||
    ! git rev-parse --verify --quiet "origin/$DEFAULT_BRANCH" >/dev/null; then
   # FAIL CLOSED: skip this bead entirely, do not recover it. Step 3's
